{{~##
   What every generated Go file starts with: the banner, the package and the imports.

   The imports are per file, and that is the whole of Go's difficulty here: an unused import
   does not compile. Kotlin could give every file the same list and suppress the warning; Go
   cannot, so each file is handed exactly the ones its own text reaches for and the generator
   works that out from the model.

   Nothing imports another generated file: they are all one package, so a table's file names
   another table's record type with no import at all. Go is the easiest of the languages on
   that axis and the hardest on this one.
##~}}
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Generated by Tabbit. DO NOT EDIT.
//
// Changes to this file may cause incorrect behavior and will be lost if the code is
// regenerated.
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

package {{ package_name }}
{{~ if imports | array.size > 0 ~}}

import (
{{~ for line in imports ~}}
	{{ line }}
{{~ end ~}}
)
{{~ end ~}}

